<title>GERMANY: SWIMMING-EUROPEAN SHORT-COURSE MEDALS TABLE.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-EUROPEAN SHORT-COURSE MEDALS TABLE.</headline>
<dateline>ROSTOCK, Germany 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medals table at the end</p>
<p>of the third day of the four-day European sprints and</p>
<p>short-course championships on Saturday:</p>
<p>		  Gold    Silver    Bronze</p>
<p> Germany	 10	   9	    8</p>
<p> Sweden	   3	   2	    1</p>
<p> Netherlands    3	   1	    0</p>
<p> Britain	  2	   4	    1</p>
<p> Czech Republic 2	   1	    2</p>
<p> Poland	   2	   0	    1</p>
<p> Italy	    2	   0	    0</p>
<p> Norway	   1	   0	    2</p>
<p> Ukraine	  1	   0	    0</p>
<p> Romania	  0	   3	    1</p>
<p> Croatia	  0	   2	    1</p>
<p> Sd    0	   1	    3</p>
<p> Slovenia	 0	   1	    2</p>
<p> Slovakia	 0	   1	    1</p>
<p> Austria	  0	   1	    0</p>
<p> Belarus	  0	   0	    1</p>
<p> Finland	  0	   0	    1</p>
<p> France	   0	   0	    1</p>
<p> Greece	   0	   0	    1</p>
<p>(Two bronzes were awarded in the men's 200 metres butterfly)</p>
